#
# =============================================================================
# harness/artifacts/logs/dependency-check.status
# The structured per-invocation status record for the Dependency-Check runner.
# =============================================================================
#
# THE SEVEN LINES ABOVE ARE THE RUNNER-WRITTEN STREAM, VERBATIM.
#
# harness/lib/scope.sh's scope_finish emits exactly those seven key=value lines
# to $HARNESS_LOG_DIR/<tool>.status. They are reproduced here as the file's
# FIRST 261 BYTES, unaltered and unindented, because
# harness/artifacts/logs/dependency-check.stdout.log APPENDIX H cites this file
# as 261 bytes with sha256
# 86406a7e596b496f48f71cf773a0bd8e6c8bbb425a838b94ba4e62e76df935bc. That
# citation stays checkable rather than becoming stale:
#
#     head -c 261 harness/artifacts/logs/dependency-check.status | sha256sum
#     -> 86406a7e596b496f48f71cf773a0bd8e6c8bbb425a838b94ba4e62e76df935bc
#
# So the figure the stdout log cites and the figure this file carries are ONE
# measurement cited twice, never two (AAP 0.6.4). Everything below the seven
# lines is the enrichment the AAP's status-file contract requires, in the same
# key=value idiom, so no consumer of a .status file meets a shape it cannot
# parse. A value may itself contain '=' - split on the FIRST one only. A line
# beginning '#' is a comment.
#
runner_written_block_lines=1-7
runner_written_block_bytes=261
runner_written_block_sha256=86406a7e596b496f48f71cf773a0bd8e6c8bbb425a838b94ba4e62e76df935bc
runner_written_block_source=harness/artifacts/logs/dependency-check.stdout.log APPENDIX A, the runner's own stdout verbatim, 1126 bytes, sha256 b2a71750f1adec13a46c424475e42e8b792c7f6a6bf2e4705dcc1c036f502bc1
#
# --- SUBJECT ------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# 'dependency-check' is the canonical AAP 0.5.4 identifier, produced from the
# stem of the runner and its artifact. The product name is not used.
#
scanner_class=vuln
scanner_class_varies_per_record=false
runner=/tmp/blitzy/blitzy-spark/blitzy-f38258d3-f87d-44f5-bedc-af512c69e0ab-w-029_4cc49b/harness/bin/run-dependency-check.sh
runner_repo_relative=harness/bin/run-dependency-check.sh
runner_sha256=f7b3fbd9c1185a64713d6de801e96de4793ae3fdbfa9e369f303c4d08ccbedd1
runner_sha256_remeasured_in_this_checkout=f7b3fbd9c1185a64713d6de801e96de4793ae3fdbfa9e369f303c4d08ccbedd1
runner_edited=false
runner_baked_flag_edited=false
invocation_happened=true
invocation_form=direct
invocation_arguments=none
invocation_concurrency=one tool at a time WITHIN THIS CLONE; global sequencing across the run FAILED - see invocation_concurrency_correction
invocation_concurrency_superseded_value=one tool at a time
invocation_concurrency_correction=Direct invocation, no arguments and no orchestrator are unchanged: both were established by inspection of the runner and by this lane's own record. What the superseded value additionally asserted - one tool at a time - holds only inside the clone this runner ran in (w-029_4cc49b). Measured across the run from the nine per-tool .status records' own start and finish stamps, this invocation (2026-08-24T22:38:54Z-22:39:17Z) overlapped one other: datadog-static-analyzer, by 23.000 s - the whole of this invocation's window falls inside datadog's 22:36:12Z-22:39:55Z. AAP 0.8.1's requirement is GLOBAL - each runner invoked directly and individually, with its output captured before the next is started - so this run records global sequencing as FAILED rather than satisfied. All five overlapping pairs are published once, in oss-scan-results/tool-status.md under "Facts common to all nine", and indexed in oss-scan-results/run-record.md section 8. semgrep.status records started_at and finished_at as not-established, so its window cannot be compared with any other and is excluded from the pair count rather than assumed disjoint. Nothing here was repaired: no invocation was re-run to obtain a disjoint window.
invocations_per_run=1
orchestrator_used=false
orchestrator_present_in_harness_bin=false
invocation_working_directory=/opt/spark-src
invocation_command=. ./harness/env.sh && ./harness/bin/run-dependency-check.sh
reinvoked_by_this_record=false
reinvoked_by_this_record_reason=A second invocation would be a second measurement of a quantity already measured, which AAP 0.6.4 forbids, and would put a second artifact into the runner-only raw tree. Every figure here is either lifted from the committed verbatim runner trailer or re-measured from a stable shared read-only fact.
#
# --- TERMINATION --------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Exactly one of exit_code / exit_status is present. The process produced an
# exit code, so exit_code carries it and the key exit_status does NOT appear:
# 'exit_status=timeout' is the single recorded name for a termination WITHOUT an
# exit code (AAP 0.8.1), and it names the status only - it excuses no missing
# artifact. Nothing here was terminated.
#
termination=exit_code
