# Artifact status and exit status are independent (AAP 0.5.4). The artifact is
# present and parses completely with no record rejected, so its status is
# 'clean' and the exit code above is recorded as a fact and used for nothing
# else. The copy at runner lines 61-63 is CONDITIONAL - the tool's report is
# copied only if it exists - so an absence was possible: the trailer would then
# have read MISSING and the absence would have needed classifying against the
# stderr capture. It printed a byte count instead.
